            "text": "{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The conversation history before this point was compacted into the following summary:\\n\\n<summary>\\n## Goal\\nFind out the current weather in Tokyo using the `get_weather` tool and report it in one short sentence.\\n\\n## Constraints & Preferences\\n- Must use `get_weather` to get the data.\\n- Answer in one short sentence.\\n\\n## Progress\\n### Done\\n- [x] Called `get_weather(city=\\\"Tokyo\\\")`, which returned: \\\"Tokyo: clear25°C, wind 10 km/h\\\".\\n- [x] Answered the user: \\\"Tokyo is clear and 25°C, with a 10 km/h wind.\\\"\\n\\n### In Progress\\n- [ ] (none)\\n\\n### Blocked\\n- (none)\\n\\n## Key Decisions\\n- **Used `get_weather` with city=\\\"Tokyo\\\"**: The user explicitly asked for this tool.\\n- **Single-sentence reply**: The user asked for a short answer.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n1. No further action needed unless the user asks a follow-up, such as the weather in another city.\\n\\n## Critical Context\\n- Tool result: Tokyo: clear, 25°C, wind 10 km/h.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\\n\\n## Original Request\\nThe user asked \\\"Is that warm? One word.\\\" They want a one-word answer. The message does not say what \\\"that\\\" refers to, and no earlier context is shown.\\n\\n## Progress So Far\\n- No work has been done. The conversation contains only the user's single message, with no assistant reply.\\n- The referent of \\\"that\\\" has not been identified or clarified.\\n\\n## Context Needed to Continue\\n- The user wants a very brief, one-word reply (presumably yes/no or similar).\\n- \\\"That\\\" is ambiguous. It may refer to something from earlier context not visible here, or to something the user has not yet specified, such as an image, object, or temperature.\\n- No other constraints, preferences, or details were given.\\n</summary>\"}]},{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[],\"output_config\":{\"effort\"